=== Prompt ===
Who is Solid Snake?

=== Response ===
Solid Snake is a fictional character and one of the main protagonists in the Metal Gear series of video games, created by Hideo Kojima. He is a member of the elite special forces unit FOXHOUND and is often depicted as a stealth operative and infiltrator. Solid Snake is known for his signature camouflage outfit, bandana, and cybernetic eye.

The character first appeared in the 1987 game Metal Gear Solid on the MSX2 computer, but gained significant popularity with the release of the 1998 PlayStation game Metal Gear Solid, which was a critical and commercial success. Solid Snake is often considered one of the most iconic video game characters of all time.

In the Metal Gear storyline, Solid Snake is a genetically-engineered soldier and the main character in several of the games, including Metal Gear Solid, Metal Gear Solid 2: Sons of Liberty, Metal Gear Solid 3: Snake Eater, Metal Gear Solid 4: Guns of the Patriots, and Metal Gear Solid V: The Phantom Pain. He is the son of Big Boss, a former member of FOXHOUND who became a major antagonist in the series. Solid Snake's mission is often to infiltrate and neutralize threats posed by advanced weaponry and rogue military forces.

